6px) 100vw, 1216px\">\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div data-particle_enable=\"false\" data-particle-mobile-disabled=\"false\" class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-37219802 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"37219802\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3b3e38f6 animated-slow elementor-invisible elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"3b3e38f6\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-settings=\"{&quot;_animation&quot;:&quot;fadeInUp&quot;}\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">735kg Reclaimed</h2>\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-7682f85b animated-slow elementor-invisible elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"7682f85b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-settings=\"{&quot;_animation&quot;:&quot;fadeInUp&quot;}\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">29 | 10 | 2025</h2>\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-56813cce animated-slow elementor-invisible elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"56813cce\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-settings=\"{&quot;_animation&quot;:&quot;fadeIn&quot;,&quot;_animation_delay&quot;:200}\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>What if every time we built a home, local communities benefitted too?</p><p> </p><p>That’s exactly what happened when Studio Rovik collaborated with Goldenb Earth Studio and opened their doors to London creatives to collect freshly excavated clay straight from their site.</p><p> </p><p>In just one week, 42 creatives signed up and 735kg of clay was saved from landfill, bagged up and taken back to studios across the city to be given a new life.</p><p> </p><p>A huge thank you to Vivek for joining Golden Earth Studio in our mission to make waste accessible. The incredible response shows just how valued secondary resources are, and why we need to do more to keep materials in circulation across construction sites.</p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>"
